# Eitri MCU firmware: X-Plus 4 TOOLHEAD ([mcu], /dev/ttyS2). Minimal Klipper/Kalico Kconfig input; expand with
# `make olddefconfig`. Identical for Klipper and Kalico (mcu/tests/test_configs.py checks both pinned trees).
#
# STATUS: UNRESOLVED (mcu/params.json). THIS FILE MUST NOT BE BUILT INTO A RELEASE and mcu/build-mcu.sh refuses to.
#   chip        STM32F103 -> CONFIG_MCU="stm32f103xe", 72 MHz (live klippy.log; may be a GD32F103 clone)
#   offset      UNSETTLED. FLASH_START_2000 below is the Katapult 8 KiB layout (application at 0x08002000) and is
#               correct ONLY IF this printer's toolhead runs Katapult. A stock bootloader would need another value
#               (0x08008000 is merely inferred from a different printer). A wrong value does not boot, and the only
#               recovery is an ST-Link. Settle it read-only first (mcu/README.md, "Open questions").
#   clock       8 MHz external crystal: HSE is certain, 8 MHz is likely
#   serial      USART1 remapped to PB7/PB6 at 500000 baud (live dictionary: RESERVE_PINS_serial=PB7,PB6)
#   not set     STM32F103GD_DISABLE_SWD (GigaDevice clones): undecided, see params.json
CONFIG_LOW_LEVEL_OPTIONS=y
CONFIG_MACH_STM32=y
CONFIG_MACH_STM32F103=y
CONFIG_STM32_FLASH_START_2000=y
CONFIG_STM32_CLOCK_REF_8M=y
CONFIG_STM32_SERIAL_USART1_ALT_PB7_PB6=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_BAUD=500000
